{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791663687,"nonce":"+QslSqLWYH2Dx0S08fArh/e8FuM=","title":"A Null\u003cInt\u003e field of an anonymous object reads as void through Dynamic and Json","message":"`var s:Null\u003cInt\u003e = -7; var o = {a: (null:Null\u003cInt\u003e), b: s};` — `o.b` prints -7, but\n`var d:Dynamic = o; d.b` prints `void` and `Json.stringify(o)` gives\n`{\"a\":null,\"b\":null}`. Same with RAYZOR_NULL_INT_BOXED=1, so it predates the unboxed\nNull\u003cInt\u003e work. The shape descriptor records the field kind from runtime_type_id, which\nmaps Optional (anything not listed) to 0 = Void (decl/anon.rs anon_field_descriptor -\u003e\nhelpers/type_ids.rs runtime_type_id `_ =\u003e 0`), so readers that consult the shape treat\nthe boxed slot as void.","files":null}]}